WEBVTT

00:23.000 --> 00:24.880
Auto-throttle, check.

00:26.390 --> 00:28.620
ALS, check.

00:29.460 --> 00:32.550
ADC 1 & 2, check.

00:33.430 --> 00:35.660
ADCS, check.

00:36.300 --> 00:39.370
AICS, check.

00:39.370 --> 00:42.130
ASE, check.

00:45.670 --> 00:48.660
Ramp to tower, B-3 is ready for takeoff.

01:48.000 --> 01:51.040
B-3, cleared for takeoff.

02:13.700 --> 02:14.700
Let's go.

02:18.380 --> 02:21.160
Let's go see Yukikaze fight.

03:26.780 --> 03:27.680
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

03:27.910 --> 03:35.300
Battle Fairy

03:27.910 --> 03:35.300
YUKIKAZE

03:42.950 --> 03:46.050
I keep telling you that thing's not necessary!

03:46.860 --> 03:51.460
You talk too much, Gunow-kun. General, what do you...

03:51.460 --> 03:53.290
Excuse the interruption, sir.

03:56.260 --> 03:58.480
B-3 has completed takeoff.

03:59.030 --> 04:02.400
May Lt. Fukai continue to observe the mission?

04:02.870 --> 04:04.050
I'll allow it.

04:04.610 --> 04:07.410
You're the one responsible for remodeling the FRX?

04:08.010 --> 04:09.950
I'm sorry, you are...?

04:09.950 --> 04:10.680
This man is...

04:10.680 --> 04:13.200
Colonel Gunow of the Systems Corps.

04:16.020 --> 04:18.850
The FRX-99 is his project.

04:18.850 --> 04:21.250
He's in charge of the unmanned fighter.

04:24.230 --> 04:26.720
Do you have some sort of explanation for me?

04:28.000 --> 04:29.890
About what, sir?

04:30.900 --> 04:33.770
Keep your cool, please, Gunow-kun.

04:35.040 --> 04:39.130
And the SAF should give a little thought to what it's done.

04:44.610 --> 04:46.110
No more...

04:50.650 --> 04:53.590
I don't want any more unfortunate victims.

04:54.970 --> 04:56.470
Excuse me.

04:59.490 --> 05:01.510
Using unmanned planes...

05:02.550 --> 05:06.260
It's the decision of GHQ and the Central Computer.

05:08.200 --> 05:13.340
I thought you'd be more cooperative, if you considered the lives of the pilots.

05:13.840 --> 05:17.040
For any other plane, it'd be all right.

05:17.780 --> 05:21.810
But B-3... Yukikaze is different!

05:22.940 --> 05:25.370
It needs a pilot!

05:26.150 --> 05:29.850
No matter what, nothing is absolutely irreplaceable.

05:30.730 --> 05:34.390
It's pointless for humans to fight in this war.

05:36.380 --> 05:38.220
Don't you agree, Major?

05:38.730 --> 05:40.220
No, I don't!

05:41.870 --> 05:43.300
In every age...

05:45.040 --> 05:48.940
...humans will always be doing the fighting.

05:50.610 --> 05:52.920
B-3 has arrived at the mission area.

05:53.730 --> 05:55.620
Point FP-27 A.

05:56.130 --> 05:59.380
Fifty-five FTS is engaging a JAM assault group.

06:03.470 --> 06:04.020
<i>Bingo!</i>

06:04.440 --> 06:07.190
<i>Outstanding! This new plane's great!</i>

06:08.900 --> 06:11.600
<i>Spencer! God dammit...!</i>

06:11.630 --> 06:14.000
<i>Griffin leader! Type 1, 6 o'clock high!</i>

06:14.000 --> 06:16.910
<i>It's locking on to you! Break left! Break left!</i>

06:16.930 --> 06:18.190
<i>I hear you!</i>

06:18.840 --> 06:19.930
<i>My engine...!</i>

06:21.840 --> 06:24.510
<i>What's wrong?! What are you doing?! Increase speed!</i>

06:27.380 --> 06:29.280
<i>Engine trouble!</i>

06:29.280 --> 06:30.730
<i>No good! I can't shake 'em!</i>

06:36.770 --> 06:39.630
<i>What the...?! What happened?!</i>

06:39.630 --> 06:42.620
<i>Griffin leader, the SAF unit shot down the JAM.</i>

06:45.700 --> 06:46.710
<i>The SAF?</i>

06:47.300 --> 06:51.300
<i>I thought they were just here to sightsee and not fight.</i>

06:54.010 --> 06:56.000
<i>We've finished the JAM off, thanks to them.</i>

06:56.340 --> 06:58.180
<i>Sector clear. RTB.</i>

07:04.700 --> 07:07.150
<i>Okay, I'm coming in on approach now.</i>

07:07.210 --> 07:11.380
<i>Griffin 1 to tower. Due to engine trouble, I'm requesting emergency landing clearance.</i>

07:11.390 --> 07:12.840
<i>Roger, Griffin 1.</i>

07:13.660 --> 07:15.160
<i>Wait, hold it.</i>

07:15.860 --> 07:18.170
<i>The SAF unit is on approach.</i>

07:18.170 --> 07:20.570
<i>Strange... It hasn't requested clearance.</i>

07:22.270 --> 07:25.170
<i>TAB-15 control to B-3.</i>

07:25.200 --> 07:27.630
<i>You are not cleared to land. Break off, B-3.</i>

07:28.180 --> 07:30.380
<i>TAB-15 control to B-3.</i>

07:30.680 --> 07:34.210
B... B-3's switched to ground attack mode...!

07:34.620 --> 07:35.370
What?!

07:36.380 --> 07:39.630
No doubt about it. It's targeting TAB-15!

07:41.820 --> 07:45.110
Major! Order B-3 to return to base at once!

07:45.430 --> 07:46.820
We can't.

07:47.160 --> 07:48.350
What do you mean?!

07:49.010 --> 07:52.430
It won't accept any external commands while on a mission!

07:53.500 --> 07:56.030
It's on full autonomous control!

07:57.470 --> 07:58.700
It can't be...

08:19.290 --> 08:20.230
The JAM...

08:24.830 --> 08:26.390
<i>That's not a landing approach...</i>

08:26.970 --> 08:30.210
- B-3, break off! B-3, do you read us?!
<i>- What's he up to? Wait, he's not...!</i>

08:30.210 --> 08:33.610
- Commander, tell TAB-15 to evacuate!
<i>- Stop him! Tower, stop him!</i>

08:34.040 --> 08:34.810
This is TAB-15 control! B-3, respond!

08:34.810 --> 08:37.200
- It's too late.
This is TAB-15 control! B-3, respond!

08:43.280 --> 08:44.410
Stop it! Don't!

08:47.520 --> 08:48.850
<i>Has he lost his mind?</i>

08:51.090 --> 08:51.630
<i>Stop...</i>

09:18.690 --> 09:19.380
Rei...?

09:22.190 --> 09:24.320
Th- There...

09:36.440 --> 09:38.340
The JAM...

09:42.340 --> 09:45.370
The JAM... are there...!

09:47.550 --> 09:49.850
CAN'T YOU SEE THEM?!

09:54.120 --> 09:57.250
Um... Are you all right? Do you feel sick?

09:58.220 --> 10:01.560
Y- Yes, I'm fine.
Anyway...

10:01.560 --> 10:03.260
Can you sign my book?

10:03.260 --> 10:05.770
I don't meet authors every day!

10:05.770 --> 10:07.720
Sure. Of course, it'd be my pleasure.

10:09.900 --> 10:12.370
"Lynn Jackson..."

10:13.430 --> 10:14.480
And who is this to?

10:14.480 --> 10:16.040
Thomas!

10:16.040 --> 10:17.340
Thomas?

10:17.410 --> 10:22.410
Yeah, my boyfriend loves this stuff. UFOs and space people and all that.

10:23.380 --> 10:24.890
I see.

10:24.890 --> 10:28.090
There you go. Give Thomas my regards, please.

10:28.090 --> 10:31.800
Thanks! I'll read it after him. See you!

10:32.060 --> 10:33.280
Bye.

10:38.930 --> 10:41.230
Space people, huh...?

10:56.070 --> 10:57.350
He doesn't remember?

10:58.790 --> 11:00.690
You mean none of that commotion...?

11:00.690 --> 11:02.220
Yeah.

11:02.220 --> 11:06.130
He said it was like he was having a bad dream.

11:08.730 --> 11:10.320
I wish it was just a dream.

11:11.300 --> 11:14.040
How are the General Staff taking it?

11:14.040 --> 11:17.310
They're livid and want to hang us all out to dry.

11:17.310 --> 11:18.610
Especially...

11:18.680 --> 11:20.240
Col. Gunow?

11:20.240 --> 11:22.850
Here's their official report.

11:26.210 --> 11:29.810
"Responsible for the accident is the Special Air Force..."

11:31.020 --> 11:33.900
"...by their deliberate sabotage of the system...?!"

11:35.260 --> 11:42.100
Fortunately, the Central Computer's judgement was that this was an "accidental weapons discharge."

11:42.100 --> 11:44.090
We barely got off the hook.

11:44.670 --> 11:48.430
Accidental...? You mean... They bought it?

11:50.370 --> 11:55.040
We also got a request to reinstate Lt. Fukai earlier than expected.

11:55.840 --> 11:59.390
Even though they're shoving the unmanned fighter program through?

11:59.750 --> 12:04.280
My guess is that they need the lieutenant.

12:04.890 --> 12:07.180
But why...?

12:07.860 --> 12:09.390
I don't know.

12:09.390 --> 12:13.800
Lt. Fukai's the only one who trusts Yukikaze more than his own eyes.

12:13.800 --> 12:16.690
Maybe it's because he believes in combat intelligence.

12:18.530 --> 12:24.770
Yukikaze... B-3 claimed TAB-15 was a JAM.

12:24.770 --> 12:29.370
Assuming those computers aren't wrong...

12:30.580 --> 12:34.910
...then it means the JAM have infiltrated the FAF.

12:44.260 --> 12:47.060
400 meters in 4 minutes, 15 seconds.

12:51.130 --> 12:54.910
From what I can see, clear physical strength isn't a problem.

13:03.640 --> 13:08.170
I've heard about you, but I never thought you were this bad.

13:09.520 --> 13:13.140
You can't fly again without my approval.

13:15.260 --> 13:18.790
3 counts of disobeying orders, 7 counts of insubordination...

13:18.790 --> 13:20.780
That's quite a record.

13:22.550 --> 13:25.530
But ever since you were assigned to the SAF...

13:25.530 --> 13:27.770
...that all miraculously stopped.

13:27.770 --> 13:30.620
Your commander must be overly kind.

13:31.570 --> 13:34.700
Or maybe you found your ideal partner?

13:39.060 --> 13:40.110
Where are you going?

13:42.220 --> 13:43.210
Hold it!

13:44.350 --> 13:45.880
I'm not finished with you!

13:46.550 --> 13:47.680
Come back here!

13:48.520 --> 13:49.790
Take your seat!

13:58.600 --> 14:00.290
To hell with your approval.

14:02.740 --> 14:06.070
Thank you, Lieutenant. That'll be all for today.

14:06.940 --> 14:10.340
I'd like to continue, though, so come back here tomorrow.

14:22.860 --> 14:23.090
The client did not exhibit strong rejection.

14:23.090 --> 14:26.390
- Captain, how did Lt. Fukai's examination go?
The client did not exhibit strong rejection.

14:26.790 --> 14:29.760
Various mental tests were conducted without his cooperation.

14:29.760 --> 14:34.430
The results stem from excessive feelings of helplessness, or possibly as a strong defense mechanism...

14:34.440 --> 14:39.930
...coupled with social skills deficit, and he shows very poor levels of CNM-CC...

14:54.890 --> 14:58.020
Its maximum turn rate has been upped 15%.

14:58.660 --> 15:01.200
Its maneuverability has been upgraded greatly.

15:02.400 --> 15:05.730
It's a real monster.

15:06.330 --> 15:09.030
So, how do you like the new Yukikaze?

15:12.010 --> 15:14.300
It's just like a JAM.

15:18.650 --> 15:22.410
This is definitely Yukikaze.

15:23.350 --> 15:27.380
Its appearance has changed because it's been reborn.

15:30.120 --> 15:32.290
And my job...

15:32.990 --> 15:35.770
...is seeing that you fly this monster.

15:38.070 --> 15:42.560
Tomorrow, you're going to be having DACT with an unmanned fighter from the Systems Corps.

15:43.970 --> 15:45.400
For what reason?

15:45.940 --> 15:48.660
Does the reason really matter to you?

15:51.250 --> 15:56.510
Has it ever mattered to you before?

15:57.590 --> 15:59.990
I'll have a talk with that doctor.

16:01.220 --> 16:02.590
Your briefing's at 06:00.

16:03.520 --> 16:06.620
Don't be late. That is all.

16:24.050 --> 16:26.340
I'm scared, too.

16:55.030 --> 16:57.030
Captain Edith Foss, was it?

16:58.260 --> 17:00.480
So, in return for her permission...

17:00.480 --> 17:02.570
...she wanted to fly with him, huh?

17:04.050 --> 17:06.350
She has the qualifications, but...

17:07.220 --> 17:10.550
Why take this little joyride now?

17:11.480 --> 17:16.300
You're aware of how sharply the casualty rate has risen lately, aren't you?

17:16.300 --> 17:20.660
Every plane being lost are new models, which were developed with great fanfare.

17:21.100 --> 17:26.000
I think those guys in Systems are trying to clear up their reputation with this.

17:48.960 --> 17:50.270
But...

18:05.010 --> 18:07.210
Okay, B-3. That's it.

18:08.820 --> 18:12.120
<i>How's it feel to get shot down three times in one day, Lieutenant?</i>

18:13.920 --> 18:15.620
It's just a game.

18:17.190 --> 18:19.710
It doesn't mean anything.

18:21.700 --> 18:24.570
<i>The only thing our unmanned fighter lacks...</i>

18:24.570 --> 18:26.860
<i>...is a sore loser function!</i>

18:27.470 --> 18:30.160
<i>I'll research that on my next project.</i>

18:31.110 --> 18:33.070
Um, sir? You're not going to say anything...?

18:33.870 --> 18:35.230
No.

18:40.770 --> 18:43.480
So, this is the future of air combat, huh?

18:43.480 --> 18:44.930
We're gonna be unemployed.

18:45.250 --> 18:46.980
Once our war with the JAM is over...

18:48.210 --> 18:50.650
...I'll also be unemployed.

18:54.560 --> 18:56.660
Air contact, bearing 6 o'clock.

18:57.430 --> 18:59.420
JAM! They're closing on us!

18:59.900 --> 19:01.800
In this area?!

19:01.800 --> 19:04.100
<i>B-3 to P-01.</i>

19:04.100 --> 19:07.470
<i>Leave the JAM to me! Retreat to a safe area at once!</i>

19:08.660 --> 19:11.450
<i>We aren't armed with live weaponry!</i>

19:11.450 --> 19:14.180
<i>I know, but we do have maneuverability!</i>

19:14.680 --> 19:17.720
<i>Ceres 2-7 to Brownie control, scramble orders!</i>

19:17.720 --> 19:21.160
<i>Vector two-niner-zero. Angels three-zero, minus two!</i>

19:21.160 --> 19:24.430
<i>Contact code "Ryvius," channel Romeo, over!</i>

19:24.430 --> 19:27.130
<i>Roger. Vector two-niner-zero. Angels three-zero!</i>

19:27.130 --> 19:29.730
<i>Contact code "Ryvius," channel Romeo!</i>

19:29.730 --> 19:32.360
Brownie just launched the SCs.

19:33.030 --> 19:36.550
Just hold out for 10... No, for 5 minutes, okay?!

19:43.910 --> 19:46.870
If you don't want to die, keep your eyes on them!

19:47.150 --> 19:48.740
R- Roger!

19:51.790 --> 19:54.010
<i>TX-1, withdrawing!</i>

19:54.290 --> 19:56.650
<i>Headed for the combat area and accelerating!</i>

19:58.530 --> 20:00.080
Assisting...?

20:07.900 --> 20:08.580
What?!

20:14.280 --> 20:15.260
What's wrong?!

20:16.040 --> 20:18.740
I'm losing engine output!

20:21.620 --> 20:23.550
Behind us! Missiles!

20:48.210 --> 20:50.480
TX-1 is headed straight for us!

20:50.480 --> 20:51.270
What?!

20:53.310 --> 20:54.450
What is it...?

21:02.820 --> 21:05.120
You... You damned...!

21:07.560 --> 21:08.770
Missiles, incoming!

21:13.230 --> 21:15.220
We just lost TS-01.

21:16.870 --> 21:19.810
TX-1 returning to support B-3.

21:20.510 --> 21:21.910
Where are those escorts?!

21:21.910 --> 21:24.450
Y- Yes, sir. Making best speed!

21:25.810 --> 21:27.710
I don't believe this!

21:29.940 --> 21:31.540
What are you trying to tell me?

21:31.550 --> 21:33.990
Behind us! They've locked on again! Shake them!

21:35.620 --> 21:36.990
Manual...?

21:49.940 --> 21:51.370
Our altitude!

21:51.370 --> 21:54.330
Capt. Foss! Can you operate the air intake control system?

21:54.740 --> 21:56.280
Huh? Y- Yes...

21:56.880 --> 21:58.750
Lock out the AICS unit!

21:58.980 --> 22:00.780
What's going on?

22:00.780 --> 22:03.280
Something's wrong with it. I'm switching us to manual!

22:03.280 --> 22:04.510
Gotcha!

22:05.420 --> 22:07.480
Lock test program into high-speed mode!

22:08.260 --> 22:09.590
High-speed mode!

22:09.860 --> 22:11.370
That should do it.

22:11.860 --> 22:13.700
No good! It won't recognize it!

22:14.330 --> 22:16.330
I'll do it! Take the stick!

22:16.330 --> 22:17.140
Huh?!

22:17.200 --> 22:19.100
Hold it steady! You have control!

22:19.370 --> 22:20.880
I... have control...

22:21.200 --> 22:23.100
Just keep us headed down!

22:39.550 --> 22:40.320
Wha...?

22:46.060 --> 22:47.760
From TX-1...?

23:07.610 --> 23:11.570
<i>Don't be afraid, Yukikaze.</i>

23:44.450 --> 23:46.650
<i>B-3, returning to base.</i>

23:50.960 --> 23:53.050
"Humans aren't needed", huh...?

23:54.630 --> 23:56.820
What was that, Jack?

23:57.230 --> 23:59.940
Col. Gunow said that to me before...

24:00.130 --> 24:03.300
...but I wonder if he really believed it.

24:05.010 --> 24:06.830
<i>Medic team 3 on runway to base.</i>

24:07.240 --> 24:10.740
<i>One casualty incurred. Transporting to medical center.</i>

24:10.770 --> 24:11.910
<i>Base here. Roger.</i>

24:11.910 --> 24:14.820
That time before... Yukikaze...

24:16.780 --> 24:19.840
...called out to me.

24:20.350 --> 24:23.260
Hm? What did you say?

24:26.830 --> 24:28.220
Nothing.

24:32.270 --> 24:34.260
What's that all about?

24:44.610 --> 24:49.610
In my dreams, it comes so clearly.

24:51.020 --> 24:56.780
Letting me embrace that day.

24:59.190 --> 25:04.060
I've seen a lot of summers off...

25:05.530 --> 25:11.760
...along the way to now.

25:13.100 --> 25:15.700
Long way to home.

25:15.500 --> 25:19.500
Because I love your smile...

25:19.370 --> 25:25.940
...that never changes.

25:27.510 --> 25:30.180
Long way to home.

25:30.050 --> 25:34.010
I'll be going back soon.

25:33.880 --> 25:37.450
I'll walk till dawn...

25:37.320 --> 25:40.420
...back to you.

25:42.090 --> 25:45.190
My sweet home!

25:45.060 --> 25:48.590
I wanna back right now!

25:49.430 --> 25:52.430
My sweet home!

25:52.340 --> 25:55.600
I wanna hold your mind!

26:00.340 --> 26:02.940
Long way to home.

26:02.810 --> 26:06.810
Let's head back right now.

26:06.680 --> 26:13.190
Because I long to see your smile.

26:14.890 --> 26:17.560
Long way to home.

26:17.360 --> 26:21.290
I'll be going back soon.

26:21.160 --> 26:24.900
I'll walk till dawn...

26:24.700 --> 26:28.530
...back to you.

27:01.380 --> 27:03.250
So, I was right.

27:03.750 --> 27:08.520
There were also signs that TAB-15's Fands were sabotaged?

27:08.710 --> 27:12.820
Right. Get that list drawn up again.

27:14.160 --> 27:17.200
Pilots, maintenance, controllers...

27:17.200 --> 27:20.260
Right. Investigate everyone.

27:25.630 --> 27:29.580
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

27:32.580 --> 27:35.680
Tomahawk John, the man with the heart of a machine.

27:35.680 --> 27:41.280
And Banshee, the gigantic flying carrier, which has suddenly started to go berserk.

27:42.180 --> 27:46.370
It is there, having just set foot aboard the mechanical fortress...

27:46.390 --> 27:50.520
...floating in the sky, that Rei beholds a terrifying sight.
